-- 1 {"commit": "637f593f50743aff545db26e9bb986aa0cd57d18", "finding": "REPORT.md and record.md were missing from the branch because the harness refused the worker's write. Both were written from the run's journal with journal-text.py, byte for byte (explorations/compile-ladder/rung-walk-open-param/REPORT.md, record.md).", "kind": "correction", "paths": ["explorations/compile-ladder/rung-walk-open-param/REPORT.md", "explorations/compile-ladder/rung-walk-open-param/record.md"], "settledBy": "The brief, 'First, the worker's report and record on the branch'"}
-- 2 {"commit": "b999851e24dec784edd63ffca52faa5a28b5667c", "finding": "The worker opened a new row, NEW-W-2, for the unwritten BIG MINMAX. Row 473 already holds that defect as its open half (explorations/fortress-gap-ledger.md:440, reproducer none). Changed: the specification now cites row~473 (Specification/basic/inference.tex:296; Specification/appendices/changes.tex:1071, :1923), REPORT.md:50,129,142,229 say row 473, and record.md drops the NEW-W-2 row. The record also gives row 473 its reproducer, XXXUnwrittenBigMinMaxWalk.fss, and names the dispatch step the worker left unlocated: OverloadedFunction.java:1755, then FTypeTuple.java:146, then FType.java:312-315.", "kind": "correction", "paths": ["Specification/basic/inference.tex", "Specification/appendices/changes.tex", "explorations/compile-ladder/rung-walk-open-param/REPORT.md", "explorations/compile-ladder/rung-walk-open-param/record.md"], "settledBy": ".claude/skills/fortress-repo/references/records.md, 'The gap ledger': 'A new issue gets a new row' (this one is not new); explorations/fortress-gap-ledger.md:440, row 473: 'Open half: with no static argument walk binds T to BOTTOM and stops at MinMaxReduction.simpleJoin'"}
-- 3 {"commit": "3f5b15ec0ca5af936b0a1c4b6f1f330dce75d80a", "finding": "Row 618's repair checks only object expressions without static parameters (BuildEnvironments.java:993; declared types :1217). An object expression inside a generic function, and a generic object, extending A and B with overlapping pick(self) still load and run A's pick, on the old code and the new. This residue had no home. Added: ProjectFortress/tests/XXXFunctionalMethodMeetGenericProviderWalk.fss and its .test, and row NEW-W-4 in record.md. The record's FACTS entry now also says what the open type does at dispatch: an open-typed declaration is the most specific, and structured types that hold the open type admit no more than before.", "kind": "correction", "paths": ["ProjectFortress/tests/XXXFunctionalMethodMeetGenericProviderWalk.fss", "ProjectFortress/tests/XXXFunctionalMethodMeetGenericProviderWalk.test", "explorations/compile-ladder/rung-walk-open-param/record.md"], "settledBy": "Specification/advanced/overloading.tex:470-471, the Meet Rule for Functional Methods: 'two functional method declarations occurring in trait or object declarations or object expressions'"}
-- 4 {"commit": "604b807a9ca1b45fadeeda57d5025e34425d7338", "finding": "REPORT.md:23 counted 11 typeMatch value checks. There are 15: grep '.typeMatch(' under interpreter/ also lists BuildEnvironments.java:229, :761, :784 and BaseEnv.java:314.", "kind": "correction", "paths": ["explorations/compile-ladder/rung-walk-open-param/REPORT.md"], "settledBy": "grep -rn '\\.typeMatch(' ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/interpreter (15 lines)"}
-- 5 {"commit": "b9d1749595cc5afb4418b4a649637a558d4ab23a", "finding": "The skeptic's programs measured two walk defects that had no rows. Each behaves the same on the base and the head. NEW-W-5: a top-level variable initialized with an object expression stops at load, 'Missing value: *objectexpr_ObjectExpr'. NEW-W-6: an object that inherits an abstract method without a body loads, and calling the method then stops with an InterpreterBug, 'has neither body nor def'. Row 614's repair now reaches NEW-W-6 through an abstract override. Added expected failures XXXObjectExpressionTopLevelVariableWalk.fss and XXXAbstractMethodUndefinedWalk.fss with its .test, and both rows in record.md.", "kind": "correction", "paths": ["ProjectFortress/tests/XXXObjectExpressionTopLevelVariableWalk.fss", "ProjectFortress/tests/XXXAbstractMethodUndefinedWalk.fss", "ProjectFortress/tests/XXXAbstractMethodUndefinedWalk.test", "explorations/compile-ladder/rung-walk-open-param/record.md"], "settledBy": "Specification/basic/expressions/object.tex:31, 'Object expressions denote object values'; Specification/basic/traits.tex:571-572, 'any object inheriting an abstract method must define a body expression for the method'"}
