== summary
"The batch is approved: I found no blocking code defect and fixed six record defects in one local commit, 79ce86fd1, \"Fold the review's corrections\". HEAD was 95bac0a25 before it. Nothing was built, run or pushed, and I did not touch the gate's folders.\n\n**The merged code.** The landed code in the three shared files is exactly the three branch patches added together, apart from the placeholders replaced by row numbers. I checked this by re-applying each branch's patch to the base and comparing with HEAD; every other file matches its branch. No two rungs change the same declaration:\n- In STypesUtil.scala, C added `providedMethods` and `providedAndOverridden` at :1622-1695, and E added `instantiateMethodApart` at :1811-1857. Neither calls the other.\n- In inference.tex, E's lists (:130-151, :266-278) and W's walk box (:300-318) are separate passages.\n\nWhat the rungs do together is already on record:\n- E's renaming makes a program that the base accepted run into C's row 651 crash. It is pinned by `XXXMethodStaticArgsBoundNamesOtherSameName` and is the curator's item E.skeptic.1.\n- C's disambiguator change reaches walk (C.judge.1).\n- W's change to how walk treats `override` in traits, and its new object-expression check, do not reach L's library, which has neither.\n\n**The skeptics' fixes.** All three defect fixes (C 79cf821d9, C 15a4be724, E 2579d7e5b) have their test failing on the worker's head and passing after the fix, in the skeptics' transcripts. The judge upheld 15a4be724, so nothing was reverted. The corrections cite sentences that settle them.\n\n**The folded record.**\n- `ledger.py check --base 83b1cae78` reports the same eight spec-path failures and one spec-section failure as the base, and the new rows 642 to 659.\n- No `NEW-` placeholder is left where a row is cited.\n- Every closed row cites a landed commit and a test that exists.\n- Every item for the curator has its PLAN entry in the right section.\n\n**What I corrected:**\n- **FACTS.md:145:** it still listed a parameter that an argument bounds only from above as left at BottomType. Row 588 fixed that in batch 10; only row 612's case remains.\n- **FACTS.md:115:** `testSpecData` is a gate step from this batch on, so the title's \"outside the gate\" no longer holds either.\n- **revival-changes.md:131:** \"36 of the ranges' declarations\" now reads 36 sites.\n- **revival-changes.md:143:** \"Walk runs them\" now names walk's stop on a method that implements an abstract declaration (row 405).\n- **FACTS-history.md:** holds the earlier text of both FACTS entries.\n- **PLAN.md:** gained review.1 (added to gather.1's entry) and review-routed.1.\n\n**Points for the curator and the next batch.**\n- **review.1:** no `ledger.py` command narrows an open row's claim. So rows 455, 611, 628 and 638 keep claims this batch made partly false. The notes on rows 615 and 405 also say something no longer true, and the notes that would correct them were refused for length.\n- **review-routed.1:** row 653's walk expected failure, a refusal at load in `ProjectFortress/tests/`, is owed to the next batch.\n\n**Specification sentences made false.** W corrected all of its own in the specification. The four skill sentences W left are gather.2. C and E list none, and E's \"incomplete\" sentence at changes.tex:1597-1599 is rightly left.\n\n**Points to report.** I list 15 in pointsReached. None holds the push.\n\n**Left for the coordinator after the gate.** The handover's \"The last landing is climb batch 10\" paragraph and PLAN's phase-3 line 9 (\"Batch 11 ... not yet drafted\") are still stale. They are the coordinator's landing-report job once the gate finishes, as in batch 10, so I did not change them."

